-- #1013 regression fixture — AN INTERFACE METHOD'S DECLARATION DEF SITE IS ITS
-- OWN NAME TOKEN.
--
-- Read test/references_fixtures/iface_method_loc/expected.golden as the
-- assertion. The load-bearing property: NO `main|method|…` DEF site may equal
-- `main|ty|Weighed`'s DEF site. (The golden carries the exact line:col pairs —
-- they are captured, not hand-counted here.)
--
-- Before the fix, `defsOfDecl`'s `DInterface` arm handed `methodDef` the DECL's
-- own `loc`, so every method inherited the INTERFACE name-token span: `weigh`
-- was recorded at `Weighed`. Against `references` that is a misleading highlight;
-- driven through `rename` it is source CORRUPTION — renaming `weigh` would
-- overwrite the interface's type name, turning `interface Weighed a` into
-- `interface newName a`. That is the #964 / #1002 class, and it was the last
-- corrupting entry left in a method's def set. The fix consumes the per-method
-- child name `Loc`s the #331 Positions channel already supplies.
--
-- `describe` is DEFAULTED deliberately: the parser emits one `IfaceMethod` per
-- CLAUSE LINE of a `where` body, so a defaulted method is TWO entries with the
-- same name (its signature and its default head), and `declPosChildLocs` emits
-- one index per the same lines — the two run 1:1. That 1:1 is what makes the
-- positional zip correct rather than merely plausible, and this fixture is where
-- it is pinned: `describe` must hold BOTH of its heads, at two DISTINCT spans,
-- and `shout`'s def must NOT be dragged onto `describe`'s default-body line by an
-- off-by-one. A regression that reverts to the decl loc collapses every method
-- onto one span and MOVES this golden.

export interface Weighed a where
  weigh : a -> Int
  describe : a -> Int
  describe x = weigh x
  shout : a -> Int

public export data Box =
  | Box

impl Weighed Box where
  weigh Box = 3
  shout Box = 4

export useIt : Int
useIt = weigh Box + describe Box + shout Box
